<article class="env-lemma" id="090R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/090R">Lemma <span data-tag="090R">10.72.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a local Noetherian ring and $M$ a nonzero finite $R$-module. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $x \in \mathfrak m$ is a nonzerodivisor on $M$, then $\text{depth}(M/xM) = \text{depth}(M) - 1$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Any $M$-regular sequence $x_1, \ldots , x_ r$ can be extended to an $M$-regular sequence of length $\text{depth}(M)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Part (2) is a formal consequence of part (1). Let $x \in R$ be as in (1). By the short exact sequence $0 \to M \to M \to M/xM \to 0$ and Lemma <a href="/tag/00LX" data-tag="00LX">10.72.6</a> we see that the depth drops by at most 1. On the other hand, if $x_1, \ldots , x_ r \in \mathfrak m$ is a regular sequence for $M/xM$, then $x, x_1, \ldots , x_ r$ is a regular sequence for $M$. Hence we see that the depth drops by at least 1. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>